question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-71ca01ef-6509-5743-9f2c-5b6fbeed89a1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-71ca01ef-6509-5743-9f2c-5b6fbeed89a1" :answer-field/id #uuid "71ca01ef-6509-5743-9f2c-5b6fbeed89a1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-4b5b5316-09c3-5fd8-9d3e-003a5bee53dc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4b5b5316-09c3-5fd8-9d3e-003a5bee53dc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b5b5316-09c3-5fd8-9d3e-003a5bee53dc" :answer/id #uuid "4b5b5316-09c3-5fd8-9d3e-003a5bee53dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3f084ce4-122d-54f2-8959-73b35064d8ae" :question/id #uuid "3f084ce4-122d-54f2-8959-73b35064d8ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-44048" :question/problem "What is the constant term in the expression $6-3x+2y?$" :question/worked-solution "The expression has three terms: $6$, $-3x$ and $2y.$ The only term that does not contain any variables is $6$, so $6$ is the constant term." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-86cdceaf-6a37-53b4-911c-e06f1fe419ae"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-86cdceaf-6a37-53b4-911c-e06f1fe419ae" :answer-field/id #uuid "86cdceaf-6a37-53b4-911c-e06f1fe419ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4538326f-9546-510f-8b5a-ac8a61f2a386" :answer-field/choices ["answer-103a6d55-5236-59cd-92c3-ab940e1f6167" "answer-a499f8a5-f3dc-5f19-b681-035708fe2d5a" "answer-b68dab54-73d3-5c81-bf2e-e357b7c61893" "answer-b0ed28c5-a6d6-5136-baa4-701b272f0f3f" "answer-4538326f-9546-510f-8b5a-ac8a61f2a386"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-103a6d55-5236-59cd-92c3-ab940e1f6167" :answer/id #uuid "103a6d55-5236-59cd-92c3-ab940e1f6167" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a499f8a5-f3dc-5f19-b681-035708fe2d5a" :answer/id #uuid "a499f8a5-f3dc-5f19-b681-035708fe2d5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b68dab54-73d3-5c81-bf2e-e357b7c61893" :answer/id #uuid "b68dab54-73d3-5c81-bf2e-e357b7c61893" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b0ed28c5-a6d6-5136-baa4-701b272f0f3f" :answer/id #uuid "b0ed28c5-a6d6-5136-baa4-701b272f0f3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4538326f-9546-510f-8b5a-ac8a61f2a386" :answer/id #uuid "4538326f-9546-510f-8b5a-ac8a61f2a386" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ebbf94e8-8bda-5e3a-9314-f9c7774a7046" :question/id #uuid "ebbf94e8-8bda-5e3a-9314-f9c7774a7046" :question/math-academy-id "q-101493" :question/problem "What is the value of the constant term in the expression $7x-\\frac{2}{9}y-3z?$" :question/worked-solution "The expression has three terms: $7x,$ $-\\frac{2}{9}y,$ and $-3z.$ Each of these terms contains a variable, so none of them are constant terms.\n\nThe constant term is missing. However, we can include it by adding zero to the expression. Rewriting the given expression as\n\n$$\n7x-\\frac{2}{9}y-3z+0,\n$$\n\nwe see that the value of the constant term is $0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0e69f4aa-cc1f-53f4-9bb4-92e5bff916a4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0e69f4aa-cc1f-53f4-9bb4-92e5bff916a4" :answer-field/id #uuid "0e69f4aa-cc1f-53f4-9bb4-92e5bff916a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a2648f19-5fca-5f9b-9748-cee1d7b80661" :answer-field/choices ["answer-af627d93-8a24-54bb-851c-b64d1659977e" "answer-9edec514-0f0b-53c6-92ff-76ee63499a6a" "answer-a2648f19-5fca-5f9b-9748-cee1d7b80661" "answer-a9f06279-62ea-59ad-a8a1-f6ae346da60d" "answer-9b2ab558-fdff-5306-b43d-cd75460508b2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af627d93-8a24-54bb-851c-b64d1659977e" :answer/id #uuid "af627d93-8a24-54bb-851c-b64d1659977e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9edec514-0f0b-53c6-92ff-76ee63499a6a" :answer/id #uuid "9edec514-0f0b-53c6-92ff-76ee63499a6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{9}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2648f19-5fca-5f9b-9748-cee1d7b80661" :answer/id #uuid "a2648f19-5fca-5f9b-9748-cee1d7b80661" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a9f06279-62ea-59ad-a8a1-f6ae346da60d" :answer/id #uuid "a9f06279-62ea-59ad-a8a1-f6ae346da60d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9b2ab558-fdff-5306-b43d-cd75460508b2" :answer/id #uuid "9b2ab558-fdff-5306-b43d-cd75460508b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2bd1aa13-179d-5d50-b799-cdeceb985d71" :question/id #uuid "2bd1aa13-179d-5d50-b799-cdeceb985d71" :question/math-academy-id "q-171468" :question/problem "The constant term in the expression $4m+7n$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The expression has two terms: \n\n$$\n4m\\,,\\,7n\n$$\n\n \n\nEach of these terms contains a variable, so none are constant.\n\nThe constant term is missing. However, we can include it by adding zero to the expression. Rewriting the given expression as\n\n$$\n4m+7n+0,\n$$\n\nwe see that the constant term is $0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-20cb68b3-1470-5d7e-933d-e77a12610b14"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-20cb68b3-1470-5d7e-933d-e77a12610b14" :answer-field/id #uuid "20cb68b3-1470-5d7e-933d-e77a12610b14" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-eacf3ffe-9baf-5cbb-9690-c854a9200472" :answer-field/choices ["answer-eacf3ffe-9baf-5cbb-9690-c854a9200472"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eacf3ffe-9baf-5cbb-9690-c854a9200472" :answer/id #uuid "eacf3ffe-9baf-5cbb-9690-c854a9200472" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186079711 :tutorial/content "The **coefficient** of a term is the number part of a term, including its sign. For instance, the coefficient of $3x$ is $3$, and the coefficient of $-5x$ is $-5.$ \n\nEvery term has a coefficient, even if it has no numerical part. For example:\n\n- The coefficient of $y$ is $1$ because $y$ is equivalent to $1y.$\n\n- The coefficient of $-z$ is $-1$ because $-z$ is equivalent to $-1z.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186079713 :tutorial/content "The **constant terms** of a linear expression are terms that contain no variables.\n\nFor example, in the expression\n\n$$\n3x + {\\color{blue}{2}} -3y +{\\color{blue}{9}},\n$$\n\nthe constant terms are ${\\color{blue}{2}}$ and ${\\color{blue}{9}}.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186079712 :tutorial/content "*If a variable is missing from an expression, then its coefficient is zero.* For example, in the expression $a+2b,$ the coefficient of $z$ is $0$ because $z$ does not appear in the expression.\n\nTo understand why the coefficient of a missing variable is always zero, remember the following:\n\n1\\. Zero times any number (or variable) is zero. So $0z$ is equal to $0.$\n\n2\\. Adding zero to an expression does not change the expression. So $a+2b$ is equal to $a+2b+0.$\n\nThus, we can rewrite $a+2b$ as \n\n$$\na+2b+0,\n$$\n\n and we can replace $0$ with $0z$ to get: \n\n$$\na+2b+0z\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we see that the coefficient of $z$ is $0.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078667 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
